<configs>

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 Kitsune Shugyo
		=====================================================================

		Two hidden permanent buffs, attached to the player in
		Config/entityclasses.xml:

		  buffShugyoPace   the practice steps (set from Settings.xml by the DLL).
		  buffShugyoLearn  the learn-by-doing triggers.

		THE PRACTICE METER: every crafting skill has ONE cvar,
		$shugyo_<skill>, counting in fractions of a level. Each source adds
		its step (1 / actions per level) and the skill levels when the meter
		reaches 1. The DLL's sources (crafting, workstations, vehicle repairs,
		wiring, looting) and magazine reads add to the SAME meter, so a skill
		fed by several sources fills one bar.

		Floats: 80 additions of 1/80 can land a hair under 1.0, so a level is
		due at 0.999, the same threshold the DLL uses (Shugyo_Practice).

		ATTRIBUTES (Phase 2) have meters too, $shugyo_<attribute>, but each
		rank costs more than the last, so their lines call the DLL's
		ShugyoPractice action instead of adding a fixed step. See ATTRIBUTE
		PRACTICE at the end of buffShugyoLearn.

		(Old saves: the Kitsune Learned Skills buffs buffKLSPace and
		 buffKLSLearn no longer exist, and the game drops unknown buffs when it
		 loads a save. The DLL carries KLS's partial counters over to the new
		 meters once per character.)

		=====================================================================
		 WHY THIS LIVES ON A BUFF (Learned Skills 0.1.0 post-mortem)
		=====================================================================

		Learned Skills 0.1.0 hung these effect groups off the weapon/tool ITEMS
		in items.xml, with a CVarCompare requirement at effect_group level.
		That crashed the game at XML load time: building an ItemValue runs
		CalcModSlotCount(), which evaluates item effect_group requirements with
		NO player entity present, so CVarCompare dereferenced null and killed
		the whole file parse. It silently took out recipes.xml, loot.xml,
		traders.xml and challenges.xml while reporting zero patch warnings.

		Two rules that keep us safe, both taken from vanilla's own patterns:
		  1. Live on a BUFF, not on an item. Buffs always run in player
		     context, so the item-construction path never touches us.
		  2. Put <requirement> INSIDE the <triggered_effect>, never on the
		     effect_group. Then it is only evaluated when the trigger fires.
	-->

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 BOOTSTRAP - how the buffs get onto EXISTING characters.
		=====================================================================

		The Buffs list on the playerMale entity class is only applied when a
		character is CREATED. Existing characters load their buff list from
		their save file, so adding a buff to the class after a character
		exists does nothing for them.

		buffStatusCheck01 is vanilla's own hidden permanent buff, attached at
		character creation, so it IS in every existing save. Piggybacking on
		it re-adds our buffs on every login. AddBuff on an already-present
		buff with stack_type ignore is a no-op, so this is safe to fire
		repeatedly. New characters additionally get the buffs instantly from
		the entityclasses.xml csv append.
	-->
	<append xpath="/buffs/buff[@name='buffStatusCheck01']">
		<effect_group>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="AddBuff" buff="buffShugyoPace"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="AddBuff" buff="buffShugyoLearn"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfRespawn"     action="AddBuff" buff="buffShugyoPace"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfRespawn"     action="AddBuff" buff="buffShugyoLearn"/>
		</effect_group>
	</append>

	<append xpath="/buffs">

		<!--
			=================================================================
			 PACE CONTROL - set it in Settings.xml (mod folder root), not here.
			=================================================================

			Each cvar = the share of a level ONE action adds to the meter.
			Settings.xml speaks in actions per level; the DLL stores
			1 / that number here.

				$shugyo_step_weapon  per kill holding that weapon type
				$shugyo_step_tool    per block hit / repair with that tool type
				$shugyo_step_use     per consumable used (food, medical)
				$shugyo_step_craft   per item crafted (DLL, per UnlockedBy skill)
				$shugyo_step_station per workstation queue completion (DLL)
				$shugyo_step_vehicle per vehicle repair (DLL)
				$shugyo_step_wire    per wire connection (DLL)
				$shugyo_step_loot    per fresh loot container opened (DLL)
				$shugyo_step_wreck   per salvage-tool hit on a vehicle wreck
				$shugyo_magazine     levels per magazine read (DLL, shared)
				$shugyo_step_attribute  1 / attribute practice points per rank
				                        step (DLL; see ATTRIBUTE PRACTICE)
				$shugyo_fatigue_points  practice points before an attribute
				                        tires (0 = off; DLL, Phase 3)
				$shugyo_rest_hours      in-game hours from tired to fresh
				$shugyo_points_after    player level past which skill points
				                        slow down (0 = off; DLL)
				$shugyo_points_every    past it, a point every N levels

			The DLL REPLACES the effect group below with the numbers from
			Settings.xml while the host loads buffs.xml, so a dedicated
			server's Settings.xml is what every client gets. The group below
			is only the SLOW fallback for a missing DLL. Editing it does
			nothing while the DLL is loaded.

			Re-applied on every world entry, so a change takes effect on your
			next login, even on an existing character.

			(Editors: XML comments cannot contain a double dash, so dividers
			 here use equals signs. Keep it that way.)
		-->
		<buff name="buffShugyoPace" hidden="true" remove_on_death="false">
			<stack_type value="ignore"/>

			<!-- SLOW fallback; overwritten from Settings.xml by the DLL. -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_weapon"  operation="set" value="0.0625"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_weapon"  operation="set" value="0.0625"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_tool"    operation="set" value="0.0125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_tool"    operation="set" value="0.0125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_use"     operation="set" value="0.125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_use"     operation="set" value="0.125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_craft"   operation="set" value="0.125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_craft"   operation="set" value="0.125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_station" operation="set" value="0.0625"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_station" operation="set" value="0.0625"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_vehicle" operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_vehicle" operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_wire"    operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_wire"    operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_loot"    operation="set" value="0.033333333"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_loot"    operation="set" value="0.033333333"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_wreck"   operation="set" value="0.0125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_wreck"   operation="set" value="0.0125"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_magazine"     operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_magazine"     operation="set" value="0.25"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_attribute" operation="set" value="0.025"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_step_attribute" operation="set" value="0.025"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_fatigue_points" operation="set" value="60"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_fatigue_points" operation="set" value="60"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_rest_hours"     operation="set" value="6"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_rest_hours"     operation="set" value="6"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_points_after"   operation="set" value="0"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_points_after"   operation="set" value="0"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_points_every"   operation="set" value="2"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$shugyo_points_every"   operation="set" value="2"/>
			</effect_group>

		</buff>

		<!--
			=================================================================
			 LEARN BY DOING - 17 sources
			=================================================================

			One line per source: the DLL's ShugyoSkill action adds one action
			of the Settings.xml source `step` to the skill's meter, levels it
			when full (with `message` and vanilla's recipe-unlock lines) and
			records the source for the Practice tab. Requirements say which
			item must be held.

			(Before 0.5.0 each source was four lines ending in vanilla's
			 AddProgressionLevel, which multiplies a +1 by the
			 PointsPerMagazine sandbox option, so a server with that above 1
			 levelled skills that many times per full meter.)

			Triggers used:
			  onSelfKilledOther      weapons. Solid, used by vanilla buffs.
			  onSelfDamagedBlock     harvesting, salvaging, wreck salvage.
			  onSelfRepairBlock      repair tools. Documented by TFP but unused
			                         in vanilla, so UNPROVEN. Safe failure.
			  onSelfPrimaryActionEnd food + medical (consuming them).
			  TriggerHasTags         on onSelfDamagedBlock checks the tags of the
			                         block that was hit (vanilla uses it for
			                         the church bell). Vehicles uses it to tell
			                         a car wreck from any other salvage hit.

			NOT COVERED HERE (handled by the DLL instead, see
			Shugyo_Learning.cs): learn by crafting (every skill), workstation
			queue completions, vehicle repairs, wire connections, spikes and
			farm-plot gateway crafts, opening fresh loot containers, and
			magazine reads (Shugyo_Sharing.cs).
		-->
		<buff name="buffShugyoLearn" hidden="true" remove_on_death="false">
			<stack_type value="ignore"/>

			<!-- clubSkill -> craftingClubs -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingClubs" step="weapon" message="Your club crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="clubSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- bladeSkill -> craftingBlades -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingBlades" step="weapon" message="Your blade crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="bladeSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- spearSkill -> craftingSpears -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingSpears" step="weapon" message="Your spear crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="spearSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- sledgeSkill -> craftingSledgehammers -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingSledgehammers" step="weapon" message="Your sledgehammer crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="sledgeSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- knuckleSkill -> craftingKnuckles -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingKnuckles" step="weapon" message="Your knuckle crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="knuckleSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- bowSkill -> craftingBows -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingBows" step="weapon" message="Your archery crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="bowSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- handgunSkill -> craftingHandguns -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingHandguns" step="weapon" message="Your handgun crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="handgunSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- shotgunSkill -> craftingShotguns -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingShotguns" step="weapon" message="Your shotgun crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="shotgunSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- rifleSkill -> craftingRifles -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingRifles" step="weapon" message="Your rifle crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="rifleSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- machinegunSkill -> craftingMachineGuns -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingMachineGuns" step="weapon" message="Your machine gun crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="machinegunSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- explosivesSkill -> craftingExplosives -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingExplosives" step="weapon" message="Your explosives crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="explosivesSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- harvestingSkill -> craftingHarvestingTools -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingHarvestingTools" step="tool" message="Your tool crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="harvestingSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- salvagingSkill -> craftingSalvageTools -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingSalvageTools" step="tool" message="Your salvage crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="salvagingSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!--
			salvagingSkill on a vehicle wreck -> craftingVehicles
			Vanilla tags every car, truck, bus and forklift wreck with
			challenge_cars (the "harvest engines from cars" challenges use
			it). A few deco blocks share the tag (air conditioners, house
			and car radiators); they count too. The same hit still feeds
			Salvage Tools through the group above.
			-->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingVehicles" step="wreck" message="Your vehicle crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="salvagingSkill"/>
					<requirement name="TriggerHasTags" tags="challenge_cars"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- repairingSkill -> craftingRepairTools -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfRepairBlock" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingRepairTools" step="tool" message="Your repair crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="repairingSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- foodSkill -> craftingFood -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfPrimaryActionEnd" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingFood" step="use" message="Your cooking crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="foodSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- medicalSkill -> craftingMedical -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfPrimaryActionEnd" action="ShugyoSkill, KitsuneShugyo" skill="craftingMedical" step="use" message="Your medical crafting knowledge grows.">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="medicalSkill"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!--
				=================================================================
				 ATTRIBUTE PRACTICE (Phase 2)
				=================================================================

				Attributes level from practice; skill points buy perks only.
				Each attribute has one meter, $shugyo_<attribute>, in fractions
				of a rank. These lines call the DLL's ShugyoPractice action
				with PRACTICE POINTS (a kill = 1); the DLL turns points into
				meter progress, because rank r -> r+1 costs r x Settings.xml's
				`attribute` points and a fixed XML step can't follow that.

				Every vanilla weapon and tool carries exactly one attribute tag
				(attPerception on rifles and wrenches, attStrength on clubs and
				pickaxes, ...), so one rule per attribute covers them all:
				  kill holding that gear       1 point x the victim's XP weight
				                               (scale="victim": walker 1,
				                               chicken 0.25, up to 2)
				  block hit holding that gear  0.1 point, not on blocks you
				                               placed this session
				                               (skip_placed; see ShugyoPlaced)
				Plus:
				  block upgrade                0.5 Strength
				  hit by a zombie, animal or
				  bandit                       0.5 Fortitude
				  healing a sprain, break or
				  infection                    10 Fortitude (appended to the
				                               vanilla injury buffs below)
				The DLL adds the rest: sneak-attack hits (Agility), fresh loot
				containers (Perception), crafting, wiring, vehicle repairs,
				reading and trading (Intellect).
			-->
			<!-- gear tagged attPerception -> Perception -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="kill" attribute="attPerception" points="1" scale="victim">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attPerception"/>
				</triggered_effect>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hit" attribute="attPerception" points="0.1" skip_placed="true">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attPerception"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- gear tagged attStrength -> Strength -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="kill" attribute="attStrength" points="1" scale="victim">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attStrength"/>
				</triggered_effect>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hit" attribute="attStrength" points="0.1" skip_placed="true">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attStrength"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- gear tagged attFortitude -> Fortitude -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="kill" attribute="attFortitude" points="1" scale="victim">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attFortitude"/>
				</triggered_effect>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hit" attribute="attFortitude" points="0.1" skip_placed="true">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attFortitude"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- gear tagged attAgility -> Agility -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="kill" attribute="attAgility" points="1" scale="victim">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attAgility"/>
				</triggered_effect>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hit" attribute="attAgility" points="0.1" skip_placed="true">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attAgility"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- gear tagged attIntellect -> Intellect -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfKilledOther" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="kill" attribute="attIntellect" points="1" scale="victim">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attIntellect"/>
				</triggered_effect>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfDamagedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hit" attribute="attIntellect" points="0.1" skip_placed="true">
					<requirement name="HoldingItemHasTags" tags="attIntellect"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- Phase 3 anti-grind: drain practice fatigue with in-game time.
			     The DLL works out the elapsed time itself, so the buff's
			     one-second tick only has to call it. -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffUpdate" action="ShugyoRest, KitsuneShugyo"/>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- Phase 3 anti-grind: remember where you place blocks, so hitting
			     them again teaches no attribute (place-and-break loops). -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfPlaceBlock" action="ShugyoPlaced, KitsuneShugyo"/>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- block upgrades -> Strength -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfUpgradedBlock" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="upgrade" attribute="attStrength" points="0.5"/>
			</effect_group>

			<!-- taking hits from zombies, animals and bandits -> Fortitude.
			     Falls, fire and cactus don't count. -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onOtherDamagedSelf" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="hurt" attribute="attFortitude" points="0.5">
					<requirement name="EntityTagCompare" target="other" tags="zombie,animal,bandit"/>
				</triggered_effect>
			</effect_group>

		</buff>

	</append>

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 FORTITUDE FROM RECOVERY (Phase 2)
		=====================================================================

		Healing an injury or infection is Fortitude practice. Each injury
		buff below ends either because it healed or because it turned into
		the next stage (sprain -> break, splint -> cast) or the player died.
		Only a heal counts: alive, and not moved on to a worse or treated
		stage. A sprain that heals by itself, a splinted or cast limb that
		mends, a cured infection.
	-->
	<append xpath="/buffs/buff[@name='buffLegSprained']">
		<effect_group>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffRemove" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="heal" attribute="attFortitude" points="10">
				<requirement name="IsAlive"/>
				<requirement name="!HasBuff" buff="buffLegBroken,buffLegSplinted,buffLegCast"/>
			</triggered_effect>
		</effect_group>
	</append>
	<append xpath="/buffs/buff[@name='buffArmSprained']">
		<effect_group>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffRemove" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="heal" attribute="attFortitude" points="10">
				<requirement name="IsAlive"/>
				<requirement name="!HasBuff" buff="buffArmBroken,buffArmSplinted,buffArmCast"/>
			</triggered_effect>
		</effect_group>
	</append>
	<append xpath="/buffs/buff[@name='buffLegSplinted']">
		<effect_group>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffRemove" action="ShugyoPractice, KitsuneShugyo" source="heal" attribute="attFortitude" points="10">
				<requirement name="IsAlive"/>
				<requirement name="!HasBuff" buff="buffLegBroken,buffLegCast"/>
			</triggered_effect>
		</effect_group>
	</append>
